diff --git a/.github/workflows/test-braindecode.yml b/.github/workflows/test-braindecode.yml
index 84290ea3ae..a20456dcf3 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/test-braindecode.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/test-braindecode.yml
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ jobs:
   test:
     name: dev ${{ matrix.os }}, py-${{ matrix.python-version }}
     runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
+    timeout-minutes: 60
     strategy:
       fail-fast: true
       matrix:
@@ -51,13 +52,35 @@ jobs:
           repository: braindecode/braindecode
           path: braindecode
 
-      - name: Install moabb, braindecode and run tests
+      - name: Install moabb and braindecode
         run: |
           uv pip install -e .
           cd braindecode && uv pip install -e .[tests]
-          echo "Running tests"
           uv pip install pytest-xdist
-          pytest test/ --quiet -n auto
+
+      # Only the MOABB integration: braindecode's full suite (~8k tests, its
+      # whole model zoo) with -n auto exhausts the 16 GB runner, which then
+      # stops with "The runner has received a shutdown signal". braindecode's
+      # own CI runs that suite.
+      - name: Run braindecode's MOABB tests
+        run: |
+          cd braindecode
+          pytest test/ --quiet -n 2 -k moabb
+
+      - name: Run braindecode's MOABB examples
+        env:
+          MPLBACKEND: Agg
+        run: |
+          cd braindecode
+          for example in \
+              examples/datasets_io/plot_moabb_dataset_example.py \
+              examples/model_building/plot_bcic_iv_2a_moabb_trial.py \
+              examples/model_building/plot_bcic_iv_2a_moabb_cropped.py \
+              examples/advanced_training/plot_moabb_benchmark.py; do
+            echo "::group::$example"
+            python "$example"
+            echo "::endgroup::"
+          done
 
       - name: Save MNE Data Cache
         if: success() && steps.cache-mne_data.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' && github.event_name == 'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/develop'
diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index 6ee13db93c..71fdb7bd9d 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -285,6 +285,7 @@ Code health
 - Share loader code across the new dataset PRs instead of private copies: :func:`~moabb.datasets.utils.download_and_extract_subject_zip` gains ``fname`` and ``redownload_corrupted`` (one warned re-download of a corrupted archive), :func:`~moabb.datasets.utils.rename_stimulus_codes` maps BrainVision ``Stimulus/S <n>`` markers to class labels, ``SetRawAnnotations`` keeps ``EDGE boundary`` markers, and the OpenNeuro raw-mirror mixin (``moabb.datasets._openneuro_mirror``) lives here once (:gh:`1200` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Modernise the BIDS layer on ``mne-bids>=0.20`` and drop MOABB workarounds it made obsolete: use :func:`mne_bids.find_matching_paths` with ``ignore_json=True`` and the public :meth:`mne_bids.BIDSPath.find_matching_sidecar` instead of a private helper, let :func:`mne_bids.write_raw_bids` serialise annotation extras into ``events.tsv`` and skip its README (``readme=False``) instead of patching both after writing, rely on mne-bids for the standard ``participants.json`` column descriptions, remove an obsolete EDF-conversion warning filter, and locate Thapa2025 files with ``find_matching_paths`` instead of probing every session/run pair (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Cap the Optuna search budget in the grid-search tests (``time_out=1``), which had doubled the ``Test`` workflow from about 23 to 47 minutes; the tests still exercise the Optuna path (:gh:`1321` proposed and measured by `Apoorva Garg`_, applied by `Bruno Aristimunha`_)
+- The ``Test-braindecode`` workflow runs braindecode's MOABB tests (``-k moabb``) and its four MOABB examples instead of braindecode's whole test suite, whose memory use with ``-n auto`` stopped the 16 GB runner ("The runner has received a shutdown signal") (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_)
 
